{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793313950,"nonce":"60rGcgSijrwDnyiYy9gYZCrhFkg=","title":"Glass panel and collected children lose joint opacity","message":"Parent: e0a7502e3e9d71bb983572df7db0033a67da1c48262e53368ae2399bc22e583a\n\nOn a71b511f a green ImageElement beneath a simple glass panel inside a 50%-opacity wrapper renders [64,191,128,255] over blue at (60,60), expected [0,128,128,255]. /private/tmp/blinc-glass-group-negative.log contains the runtime failure. The material pass is separate from its child foreground/collected image, and the planner excludes the material owner. A shared visual group must composite the panel and supported children before applying opacity/effects, preserving backdrop coordinates, clips and callback execution. Keep unsupported nested glass, portal/flow/3D combinations explicit; do not claim those safe based on metadata.","files":null}]}